==Battleground==
*1 [[Aku Cyclone]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Dark Cyclone]] spawns after 42 seconds<sup>1,260f</sup>.
*1 [[White Cyclone]] spawns after 44 seconds<sup>1,320f</sup>.
*1 [[Red Cyclone]] spawns after 46 seconds<sup>1,380f</sup>.
*1 [[Cosmic Cyclone]] spawns after 48 seconds<sup>1,440f</sup>.
*1 [[Primeval Cyclone]] spawns after 146.67 seconds<sup>4,400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The omission of [[Zyclone]] and [[Divine Cyclone]] definitely eases the stage, but Aku Cyclone and Primeval Cyclone can really cause some serious trouble since they both aren't Floating enemies. Aku Cyclone is arguably easier as its health isn't all that high with the abundance of Shield Piercing units, but Primeval Cyclone can be a rather dangerous threat since it has massive health, one knockback, and pushes rapidly when its strengthen activates. While it's often mandatory to dedicate many units for most of the other threats, it would be definitely wise to reserve a couple of Anti-Relic specialists. To a lesser extent, Cosmic Cyclone can also pose a threat due to its surprisingly high range.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]]/[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] - Without Sanzo's AOE slow against Floating enemies at close range and Seafarer's Freeze against Aliens, defeating the first few Cyclones could be outright impossible.
*[[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] - A spammable attacker whose strong ability against Floating gives her the upper hand against most of the threats, while her range even allows her to batter down Aku Cyclone. However, assistance from other units might be necessary against Cosmic Cyclone and Primeval Cyclone, as Primeval Cyclone eats through everything at lightspeed when left unchecked, and she only barely outranges Cosmic Cyclone.
*[[Shield Piercing]] Units - Units such as [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Evil Aku Researcher]], [[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]] or [[Pied Piper Cat (Rare Cat)|Brass Cat]] are almost mandatory due to the presence of Aku Cyclone.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] - Despite being a fast rusher with short range, Fishman is actually able to outrange most of the threats and put its Massive Damage ability against Floating enemies to good use. Destroying one of the Cyclones early can already grant a massive resource boost, making the rest of the stage that much easier.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Mystic Uril]] - Uril is a staple in many strategies due to his slow ability against Relics and Surges. He shouldn't be used alone, but a fair bit of support will allow him to greatly impede Primeval Cyclone, enough for other units to swarm and destroy it quickly. Once Uril's True Form has been unlocked after [[Infernal Tower/Floor 50|F50]], he can even be used against Aku Cyclone in future replays.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]] - If one happens to own this Ultra Form, they can be of great help. They can dish out great damage output from a safe range, and provide CC to all of the threats in the stage (except Aku Cyclone and Primeval Cyclone) in the form of Knockback and Freeze, which is only amplified by their level 10 [[Wave Attack]].
*[[Empress Chronos (Uber Rare Cat)|Empress Chronos]] - Chronos' closely-spaced LD multi-hits Freeze traited enemies for 1 second each. Provided if Aku Cyclone's Shield is dealt with and other supplementary CC units are factored in, Chronos can greatly impede their advance and significantly expand windows of opportunity.
*[[Miko Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Mitama the Oracle]] - With LD slow and resistance against traited enemies, Mitama's decent uptime can slow the entire cyclone cluster, allowing for safe accumulation of other attackers.
*[[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan Pasalan]] - This stage contains a handful of durable, short-ranged single threats, and since other specialists will be doing most of the work, Lufalan can actually get a few opportunities to hit them for extreme damage while its long range keeps it safe, offsetting its fragility entirely. If done correctly, it could quickly take out Cosmic Cyclone and assist in demolishing Primeval Cyclone.
*[[Netherworld Nymph Lunacia (Uber Rare Cat)|Netherworld Nymph Lunacia]] - Weakens all the Cyclones barring Primeval, which allows your meatshields to survive for longer. She also has some good DPS against them due to her Strong Vs. Floating, and has a chance to pierce Aku Cyclone's shield, allowing your other units to CC it.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Celestial Child Luna]] - Freezes some of the more dangerous cyclones, as well as dealing decent damage towards them. Of course, she requires support to deal with the other 3, so she should not be relied on alone.
*[[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]] - Having massive damage against all traits at extreme range with a very small blindspot, this unit can be all the DPS needed to tackle every threat conceivable when backed by support.
*[[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Extinction Phono]] - Despite this unit's horrendous slow uptime against all enemies, its excellent LD reach hits much further than its standing range to provide support with decent DPS itself.
*[[Saber (Uber Rare Cat)|Saber]] - This collab unit is one of the best Ubers to bring here because she can deal with almost everything here plus Relic with her Talents. Her Massive Damage, DPS and Long Distance attacks will definitely take care of all of the enemies leaving Aku Cyclone alone to be dealt with. And easing the Primeval Cyclone fight by a lot through pure brute force. Just make sure to protect her well and you can win pretty easily.

